# Terminfo source for Tessera (ADR 0005).
#
# This entry is self-contained on purpose: it never says `use=xterm-256color`,
# so it compiles on a remote host whose terminfo database is empty or ancient.
# It describes an xterm-compatible terminal plus the extensions Tessera
# implements. Extended (user-defined) capabilities need `tic -x`; without the
# flag they are silently dropped, so always compile with it:
#
#     tic -x -o ~/.terminfo shell-integration/terminfo/tessera.terminfo
#
# Extended capability glossary (names are the de facto standard shared with
# kitty, WezTerm, foot, ghostty and tmux):
#
#   fullkbd   kitty keyboard protocol (CSI > flags u / CSI < u / CSI ? u)
#   Smulx     styled underline: CSI 4:n m (0 none, 1 straight, 2 double,
#             3 curly, 4 dotted, 5 dashed)
#   Setulc    underline colour: CSI 58:2::r:g:b m  (parameter is an RGB
#             integer, split into three bytes)
#   Su        boolean advertising Smulx/Setulc (vim, neovim)
#   Tc        24-bit colour (tmux); setrgbf/setrgbb are the ncurses spellings
#   RGB is not set and colors stays 256 so `pairs` fits in a 16-bit slot for
#   old ncurses builds; applications detect direct colour via Tc/COLORTERM.
#   Sync      synchronized output, DCS form (tmux, neovim)
#   XF        focus-in/out reporting (kxIN / kxOUT)
#   Ss/Se     cursor shape (DECSCUSR)
#   Cs/Cr     cursor colour (OSC 12 / OSC 112)
#   Ms        clipboard (OSC 52)
#   smol/rmol overline (SGR 53 / 55)
#   BE/BD/PS/PE bracketed paste
#   XM        SGR mouse (1006)
#   XR/RV     XTVERSION / primary DA queries
#   E3        clear scrollback
#   rep       REP, repeat preceding character
#
# Everything else is the stock xterm-256color behaviour, including the
# modifier-encoded key tables (kUP3 … kUP7 etc.) that ncurses and tmux read.

tessera|Tessera terminal emulator,
	am, bce, ccc, km, mc5i, mir, msgr, npc, xenl,
	AX, XF, XT, Su, Tc, fullkbd,
	colors#256, cols#80, it#8, lines#24, pairs#32767,
